embers fondly was  when he had to give a speech he didn't  know the lines to  on the days of the great hall to solve  this the crew ended up putting his lines  on big boards at the end of the hall  so gambin could read off them the late  alan rickman almost dropped out of the  role of snape after the first couple of  films  but a conversation with jk rowling  changed all that  rowling whispered always to rickman and  gave him the backstory he needed in  order to truly master the role  after that conversation rickman would  even assure the directors that he knew  much more about the character than  even they did rickman also enjoyed one  of his final scenes with ray fines in  deathly hallows part 2  where he was able to put down his wand  and just talk  while you live the elder wand cannot  truly  be mine robbie coltrane was gracious to  play such a lovable character in hagrid  after making a career off of playing  hard-edged characters  coltrane's favorite moment occurred in  the sorcerer's stone where norbert the  baby  dragon breeds fire onto hagrid's beard  you have to be trained up a bit of  course  natalia tenna who played hufflepuff  nymphadora tonks said that being able to  fly on a broom  was her favorite part of filming you're  in like this massive  green room on this movable thing and  there's like these two kind of sexy  strong guys  blowing wind at you unlike some of his  fellow cast members  david thulis's favorite scene wasn't one  that he was in  his favorite scene was the opening of  prisoner of azkaban  where harry uses a spell that causes ant  marge to blow up like a balloon  [Music]  jason isaac's favorite scene was one of  the first scenes he ever  shot with richard harrison with young 11  year old daniel  and the day that i realized that i could  wave my hand and doors would shut  the late helen mcrory recalled being in  awe of the final showdown between harry  and voldemort and called it an  extraordinary experience  she said we filmed it in re